# Thespian's Stage becomes a copy of Dark Depths with no ice counters, and Bot1 keeps the original Dark Depths under the legend
# rule (CR 704.5j): the Stage goes to the graveyard. Its state trigger had triggered the moment the Stage was a Dark Depths with
# no ice counters, before state-based actions were checked (CR 603.8, 704.3), so it is put on the stack all the same (CR
# 113.7a: an ability exists apart from its source). It resolves and can't sacrifice the Stage, now a new object (CR 400.7), so
# "If you do" makes no Marit Lage. The real Dark Depths keeps its ten ice counters.

[Bot1 Deck]
Dark Depths
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Thespian's Stage
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Dark Depths.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Thespian's Stage.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Depths; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Dark Depths#1)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Thespian's Stage
? Stack = Dark Depths
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Dark Depths; Mox Pearl; Sol Ring
Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Depths.Counters.Ice = 10
Bot1.Graveyard = Thespian's Stage
Stack.Count = 0
